        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ploughs. अर्कमूलस्य—The root of the Arka ( calatropis Gigantia,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "रुई in Maráthi ) is a worthless plant. Cf. the proverb अर्के चेन्मधु",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "विन्देत किमर्थं पर्वतं व्रजेत् । कर्पूरखण्डान्—( खण्ड m =a collection )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "a collection of karpura plants. वृतिं—from वृ to cover, to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "surround+ति ( क्तिन् ) what surrounds, a hedge. कोद्रवाणाम्—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "कोद्रव is a kind of very poor and coarse grain, and is commonly",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "known as हरीक कर्मभूमि—lit. the land of religious rites i. e.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "this world as opposed to भोगभूमि ( such as Swarga, the world",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "of the moon &c. ). ‘The idea is somewhat similar to that of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "Bishop Butler who calls this a world for man’s probatin.’—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "Telang. Hindu writers refer by this to India ( the land of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "Bharata भरतवर्ष ) which is the fittest land for the performance",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "of religious rites. It is laid down in S'ruti ( see Chhánd. Up. )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "that men repair to the world of the moon &c. to reap the bene-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "fits of their meritorious deeds; and when the fund of happiness",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "laid in store there for them is exhausted they come down again",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 19,
          "text": "to this world of mortals to perform karman. Cf. कर्मभूमिभूतेऽ-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 20,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 21,
          "text": "स्मिन् भारते वर्षे । Kad. p 457. कर्मभूमिमिमां प्राप्य कर्तव्यं कर्म यच्छुभम्’ ।",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 22,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 23,
          "text": "Rámá. Ayod. K. कर्मभूमिरियं ब्रह्मन् फलभूमिरसौ मता । quoted by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 24,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 25,
          "text": "Mr. Telang from Muir. V. 324. तपस्—is used here in a wider",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 26,
          "text": "sense; as meaning the performance of one’s religious duties",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 27,
          "text": "of all sorts, necessary to elevate one to heaven. The idea ex-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 28,
          "text": "pressed here is this. Men, who waste the opportunity of securing",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 29,
          "text": "heaven ( or moksha' ) by practising tapas, given to them by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 30,
          "text": "birth in this world, are as foolish as one who &c. The fig. is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 31,
          "text": "मालानिदर्शना.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 107 The moral Mr. Telang draws from this verse is “A",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "man may do the most difficult and dangerous things in order",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "to do what is fated not to happen, or to avoid what is fated to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "happen. But he will fail.” There is no reference in this verse,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "however, to “ avoiding what is fated to happen.” The verse",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "says that although a man may dive into the sea ( for pearls or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "other gems), go to the golden mountain, Meru, conquer enemies",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "in battle, or carry on trade and so forth, no wealth comes to",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
